## HEAD  (2026-07-18)

Initial standardized snapshot at this commit; no predecessor entry.
VisualWebArena (910 tasks = WebArena stack + Classifieds container) runs the
strict read/write split via
`devs/exps/eval/browsergym.visualwebarena/run.sh`: a fully-parallel READ pass
over non-mutating tasks, then a serial (concurrency 1) WRITE pass over mutating
tasks in **topological** `depends_on` order, then a read-only RECONCILE pass
that rebuilds one combined `summary.json` over all tasks that were supposed to
run. Unlike WebArena, VWA's `depends_on` is NOT monotonic in task-id (346 of the
533 mutating tasks have a parent registered later), so the write pass is driven
by a generated prompt-data parquet whose row order is the topological sort.
Default mode is `goal_image.yaml` (screenshot + coord; goal image(s) re-shown
each turn); `mixed.yaml` (text + AXTree bid-mode + goal image(s)) and `som.yaml`
(qwen only) selectable via `EVAL_MODE`. The LLM-judge subset and classifieds
`require_reset` tasks run by default (need `OPENAI_API_KEY` +
`VWA_CLASSIFIEDS_RESET_TOKEN` on the env-server); no gpt configs exist for VWA.
